  "body": "Welcome to 18A Brandon Road, Manly, an opportunity to secure your own slice of this popular coastal community, where convenience, lifestyle and affordability come together.\r\n\r\nPerfectly suited to first-home buyers, young couples, small families or investors looking for a smart addition to their portfolio, this appealing two-bedroom home offers an easy-care lifestyle in a location that continues to capture the hearts of buyers.\r\n\r\nOne of the real highlights here is the north-facing backyard. Enjoy the sunshine, create your own outdoor retreat, fire up the barbecue with friends or simply unwind with a coffee in the fresh air. With low-maintenance outdoor spaces, you'll have more time to enjoy what matters, rather than spending your weekends on upkeep. \r\n\r\nWith new carpet, LED lights and a full interior repaint, it is move-in ready. Add the convenience of two off-street carparks, and you've got the practical essentials covered.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's the location! Manly is all about embracing an easygoing coastal lifestyle, with beautiful beaches, seaside walks and the welcoming village atmosphere all close at hand. Whether it's a morning stroll along the beach, a coffee at your favourite local café, a bite to eat with friends or a quick trip to the shops for everyday essentials, you'll love having so much within easy reach. The surrounding beaches provide the perfect backdrop for weekend swims, sunset walks and lazy summer afternoons, while the wider Peninsula offers plenty of opportunities to get outdoors and make the most of what the coast has to offer.\r\n\r\nPacked with potential, this easy-care home is all about making smart buying decisions without sacrificing the lifestyle you want. It may not be the biggest home on the block, but it offers something just as valuable: an affordable opportunity to get started, enjoy the sunshine and make the most of everything Manly has to offer.\r\n\r\nIf you've been waiting for the right opportunity to make your move, this could be the one. Easy-care living, a sunny north-facing backyard, and a fantastic coastal location, all wrapped up in a home that makes getting onto the property ladder feel a little more achievable.",
